The Prouhet-Thue-Morse sequence, denoted as $(t_n)_{n\geq 0}$, is defined by $t_n = 0$ if the sum of the binary digits of $n$ is even, and $t_n = 1$ otherwise. This work examines binary motifs of the form $0^a1^b$ within this sequence. We establish that for any positive integers $a$ and $b$, the motif $0^a1^b$ appears in $(t_n)_{n\geq 0}$ precisely when $a$ is a multiple of $2^{
u_2(b)+1}$ and $b$ is a multiple of $2^{
u_2(a)+1}$, where $
u_2(n)$ represents the exponent of the highest power of 2 dividing $n$. Furthermore, we provide an explicit formula for the count of occurrences of $0^a1^b$ within the initial $N$ terms of the sequence.
